@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `il-interpretation-time`
IMPORT domain
IMPORT `g2-validity`
IMPORT `g2-conditions`

-- g2-temporary-licence.l4: section 9 of the Regulation of Engagement in Work on Refrigeration or Air-Conditioning Systems Law
-- 5785-2025, the temporary licence of a foreign expert.
--
-- IMPORTS.  prelude, daydate, il-interpretation-time, domain, and the group's own g2-validity and g2-conditions (for the
-- alternative reading that still asks s 6(a)(1) and (3) of the expert).  No other group's module.
--
-- INPUTS.  `the fee was paid in full` (IP11, group G8: regulation 2(d) fixes a fee for a temporary licence or its renewal
-- and regulation 4 bars the Registrar from giving or renewing a licence for which a fee is fixed unless it is paid); the
-- Registrar's recognition of the expert (s 9(a)(3), IP17).  The facts about a foreign expert are NOT in domain.l4: the record
-- `Foreign expert's application under section 9` below is a LOCAL STAND-IN, listed under "nouns requests" in FRAGMENT-G2.md, for the INTEGRATOR
-- to move into domain.l4 if it wishes.
--
-- WHAT IS ENCODED.  s 9(a): a power of the Registrar ("may") to give a temporary licence of grade 3, for a period not
-- exceeding one year, to an applicant from a foreign state who meets three conditions; s 9(b): a power to renew it for two
-- further periods of up to one year each.  Both are regulative MAY rules typed by the role that acts and what is done, with
-- the conditions and the term's cap as computable conditions; the Registrar chooses the term (an input).
--
-- PERIODS (the fleet's ruling 4).  The term of a temporary licence and of each renewal is a period of VALIDITY (kind V): IL
-- s 10(b), "one year after an event", the last day inside the period; IL s 10(c) is NOT applied, and the alternative is callable.
-- The six preceding years of s 9(a)(2) are counted BACKWARDS from the application (kind B): Interpretation Law s 10 does not
-- cover them (it speaks of periods from a day or after an event), so the time module is not used, plain date comparison is.
--
-- FORKS REGISTERED IN THIS MODULE (full text in FRAGMENT-G2.md section 2):
--   FT1  s 9(a) "notwithstanding ss 6 and 8" displaces ALL of s 6 and s 8.  TAKEN: the expert need meet only s 9(a)(1) to (3) (and
--        be from a foreign state); s 6(a)(1) (adult), (2) (citizen or resident: impossible for a foreign expert) and (3) (no
--        disqualifying offence) are not asked.  ALTERNATIVE: s 6(a)(1) and (3) are still asked.
--   FT2  The cap of "a period not exceeding one year" (kind V): TAKEN: the last day of the term is no later than the last day of
--        one year after the day of the grant (IL s 10(b)); ALTERNATIVE: IL s 10(c) applied to that last day.
--   FT3  The renewal's one-year cap (P5): TAKEN: counted from the last day of the term it renews (the terms run consecutively);
--        ALTERNATIVE: counted from the day of the renewal.
--   FT4  s 9(a)(2) "in the six years preceding the filing of the application" (kind B): TAKEN: from the same calendar date six
--        years before the application up to the day BEFORE it; ALTERNATIVE: the application day itself counts.
--   FT5  s 9(a)(1) "a system whose cooling capacity is above 70 kW": TAKEN a single invited system (the text says "a
--        system") and strictly above 70, so a system of exactly 70 kW (a grade 2 system, s 2) does not qualify; the plural "works" is
--        read as works on that system.
--   FT6  s 9(a)(2) "similar" systems and "authorised" abroad are facts supplied with the application (not the Registrar's
--        opinion, which the text reserves for (3)).

§ `Section 9 — a temporary licence for a foreign expert`

@desc The acts of the Registrar under section 9: giving a temporary licence of grade 3 and renewing it, each with the last day of the term
DECLARE `An act under section 9` IS ONE OF
    `grant a temporary grade 3 licence for a term ending on` HAS `the last day of the term` IS A DATE
    `renew a temporary licence for a term ending on` HAS `the last day of the renewed term` IS A DATE

@desc One piece of work the foreign expert did abroad, with the fact that matters to s 9(a)(2): whether it was on systems similar to those the expert was invited to work on
DECLARE `Work done abroad by a foreign expert under section 9` HAS
    `the work` IS A `Work item` @desc The installation or maintenance: who did it, which kind of job, the system and the day
    `on a system similar to the systems the expert was invited to work on` IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the system was similar to the systems the expert was invited to Israel to install or maintain

@desc A foreign expert's application for a temporary licence: the facts s 9(a) asks of the applicant (a local stand-in for domain.l4)
DECLARE `Foreign expert's application under section 9` HAS
    `the application` IS AN Application @desc The application: who applies and the day it was made
    `the applicant comes from a foreign state` IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the applicant is from a foreign state (s 9(a), lead-in)
    `the system the expert was invited to work on` IS A `Cooling system` @desc The system for whose installation or maintenance the expert was invited to Israel
    `authorised to do such work in a foreign state` IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the applicant is authorised to install or maintain refrigeration or air-conditioning systems in a foreign state
    `work done abroad` IS A LIST OF `Work done abroad by a foreign expert under section 9` @desc The installations and maintenance the applicant did abroad

-- s 9(a)(1): "he was invited to Israel to do works on a refrigeration or air-conditioning system whose cooling capacity is
-- above 70 kilowatts" (the lead-in of s 9(a) also asks that the applicant be from a foreign state).
-- src:104 | {{ח:תתת|(1)}} הוא הוזמן לישראל לשם ביצוע עבודות במערכת קירור או מיזוג אוויר שתפוקת הקירור שלה מעל 70 קילו־ואט;
@ref s 9(a)(1): invited to Israel for work on a system above 70 kW (src:104)
GIVEN expert IS A `Foreign expert's application under section 9`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 9(a)(1) — the expert was invited to work on a system above 70 kW` expert MEANS
    expert's `the system the expert was invited to work on`'s `cooling capacity in kilowatts` GREATER THAN 70

-- s 9(a)(2), the six years before the application.  KIND B: counted backwards, outside Interpretation Law s 10.  The first day
-- is the same calendar date six years before the day of the application (a 29 February rolls to 1 March); the window ends the day
-- before the application (FT4).  No add years / add months is used: the year is decremented on the components.
@ref s 9(a)(2): the six years preceding the application (kind B, outside IL s 10)
GIVEN day IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 9(a)(2) — the first day of the six years before the application made on` day MEANS
    Date (DATE_DAY day) (DATE_MONTH day) (DATE_YEAR day MINUS 6)

@ref s 9(a)(2): the six years preceding the application (kind B, outside IL s 10)
GIVEN work IS A `Work done abroad by a foreign expert under section 9`
      day IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 9(a)(2) — the work` work `was done in the six years before the application made on` day MEANS
        work's `the work`'s `date performed` AT LEAST `s 9(a)(2) — the first day of the six years before the application made on` day
    AND work's `the work`'s `date performed` LESS THAN day

-- FT4, the alternative: the application day counts.
@ref s 9(a)(2): the six years preceding the application (kind B, outside IL s 10)
GIVEN work IS A `Work done abroad by a foreign expert under section 9`
      day IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 9(a)(2) (the application day counts) — the work` work `was done in the six years up to the application made on` day MEANS
        work's `the work`'s `date performed` AT LEAST `s 9(a)(2) — the first day of the six years before the application made on` day
    AND work's `the work`'s `date performed` AT MOST day

-- src:105 | {{ח:תתת|(2)}} הוא מוסמך לבצע עבודות במערכות קירור או מיזוג אוויר במדינת חוץ וביצע בשש השנים שקדמו להגשת הבקשה לרישיון זמני, התקנה או תחזוקה של מערכות קירור או מיזוג אוויר דומות למערכות שלשם התקנתן או תחזוקתן הוזמן לישראל;
@ref s 9(a)(2): authorised abroad, and in the six preceding years did installation or maintenance of similar systems (src:105)
GIVEN expert IS A `Foreign expert's application under section 9`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 9(a)(2) — the expert is authorised abroad and did similar work in the six preceding years` expert MEANS
        expert's `authorised to do such work in a foreign state`
    AND any (GIVEN work YIELD
                    work's `on a system similar to the systems the expert was invited to work on`
                AND `s 9(a)(2) — the work` work `was done in the six years before the application made on` (expert's `the application`'s `the day of the application`))
            (expert's `work done abroad`)

@ref s 9(a)(2), the application day counted (src:105)
GIVEN expert IS A `Foreign expert's application under section 9`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 9(a)(2) (the application day counts) — the expert is authorised abroad and did similar work in the six preceding years` expert MEANS
        expert's `authorised to do such work in a foreign state`
    AND any (GIVEN work YIELD
                    work's `on a system similar to the systems the expert was invited to work on`
                AND `s 9(a)(2) (the application day counts) — the work` work `was done in the six years up to the application made on` (expert's `the application`'s `the day of the application`))
            (expert's `work done abroad`)

-- s 9(a)(3): "the Registrar recognised him as a person of repute and a renowned expert in his field" - the Registrar's
-- opinion, an input (IP17).
-- src:106 | {{ח:תתת|(3)}} הרשם הכיר בו כבעל מוניטין וכמומחה בעל שם בתחומו.
@ref s 9(a)(3): the Registrar recognised the expert as of repute and a renowned expert in the field (src:106)
GIVEN `in the Registrar's opinion the expert is of repute and a renowned expert in the field` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 9(a)(3) — the Registrar recognised the expert as of repute and renowned in the field` `in the Registrar's opinion the expert is of repute and a renowned expert in the field` MEANS
    `in the Registrar's opinion the expert is of repute and a renowned expert in the field`

-- src:103 | {{ח:תת|(א)}} על אף האמור {{ח:פנימי|סעיף 6|בסעיפים 6}} {{ח:פנימי|סעיף 8|ו־8}}, הרשם רשאי לתת רישיון דרגה 3 זמני, למבקש ממדינת חוץ שמתקיימים לגביו התנאים המנויים להלן (בסעיף זה – מומחה זר), לתקופה שלא תעלה על שנה (בסעיף זה – רישיון זמני):
@ref s 9(a): an applicant from a foreign state who meets the conditions listed (src:103)
GIVEN expert IS A `Foreign expert's application under section 9`
      `in the Registrar's opinion the expert is of repute and a renowned expert in the field` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 9(a) — the applicant is a foreign expert meeting conditions (1) to (3)` expert `in the Registrar's opinion the expert is of repute and a renowned expert in the field` MEANS
        expert's `the applicant comes from a foreign state`
    AND `s 9(a)(1) — the expert was invited to work on a system above 70 kW` expert
    AND `s 9(a)(2) — the expert is authorised abroad and did similar work in the six preceding years` expert
    AND `s 9(a)(3) — the Registrar recognised the expert as of repute and renowned in the field` `in the Registrar's opinion the expert is of repute and a renowned expert in the field`

-- FT1, the alternative: s 6(a)(1) and (3) are still asked of the foreign expert.
@ref s 9(a)
GIVEN expert IS A `Foreign expert's application under section 9`
      `in the Registrar's opinion the expert is of repute and a renowned expert in the field` IS A BOOLEAN
      `in the Registrar's opinion an offence the applicant was convicted of or is charged with makes the applicant unfit to be a licensee` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 9(a) (also asking s 6(a)(1) and (3)) — the applicant is a foreign expert meeting conditions (1) to (3)` expert `in the Registrar's opinion the expert is of repute and a renowned expert in the field` `in the Registrar's opinion an offence the applicant was convicted of or is charged with makes the applicant unfit to be a licensee` MEANS
        `s 9(a) — the applicant is a foreign expert meeting conditions (1) to (3)` expert `in the Registrar's opinion the expert is of repute and a renowned expert in the field`
    AND `s 6(a)(1) — the applicant is of full age` (expert's `the application`)
    AND `s 6(a)(3) — no disqualifying conviction or pending indictment` (expert's `the application`) `in the Registrar's opinion an offence the applicant was convicted of or is charged with makes the applicant unfit to be a licensee`

-- The term.  FT2.  "for a period not exceeding one year": the last day of the term may be no later than the last day of one
-- year after the day of the grant (IL s 10(b)); IL s 10(c) is not applied (kind V).
-- src:103 | {{ח:תת|(א)}} על אף האמור {{ח:פנימי|סעיף 6|בסעיפים 6}} {{ח:פנימי|סעיף 8|ו־8}}, הרשם רשאי לתת רישיון דרגה 3 זמני, למבקש ממדינת חוץ שמתקיימים לגביו התנאים המנויים להלן (בסעיף זה – מומחה זר), לתקופה שלא תעלה על שנה (בסעיף זה – רישיון זמני):
@ref s 9(a): a temporary licence for a period not exceeding one year (src:103)
@export The latest last day a temporary licence granted on the given day may have: one year after that day (Interpretation Law s 10(b)), s 9(a)
GIVEN `the day of the grant` IS A DATE @desc The day the temporary licence is granted
GIVETH A DATE
`s 9(a) — the latest last day of a temporary licence granted on` `the day of the grant` MEANS
    `s 10(b) — the last day of a period of` 1 `years after an event on` `the day of the grant`

@ref s 9(a): a temporary licence for a period not exceeding one year, with Interpretation Law s 10(c) applied (src:103)
GIVEN `the day of the grant` IS A DATE
      `the calendar of rest days` IS A `Calendar of rest days`
GIVETH A DATE
`s 9(a) (Interpretation Law s 10(c) applied) — the latest last day of a temporary licence granted on` `the day of the grant` `, with` `the calendar of rest days` MEANS
    `s 10(b), (c) — the last day of a period of` 1 `years after an event on` `the day of the grant`
        `, when days of rest, recess or holiday are`
        (`days of rest, recess or holiday listed in` (`the calendar of rest days`'s `days of rest, recess or holiday`))

@ref s 9(a)
GIVEN `the day of the grant` IS A DATE
      `the last day of the term` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 9(a) — the term of a temporary licence granted on` `the day of the grant` `and ending on` `the last day of the term` `does not exceed one year` MEANS
    `the last day of the term` AT MOST `s 9(a) — the latest last day of a temporary licence granted on` `the day of the grant`

-- The power.  The Registrar chooses the term (the act carries its last day); a term over the cap is not an exercise of the power.
-- FC1's fee condition applies in the same way as for s 6(a).
-- src:103 | {{ח:תת|(א)}} על אף האמור {{ח:פנימי|סעיף 6|בסעיפים 6}} {{ח:פנימי|סעיף 8|ו־8}}, הרשם רשאי לתת רישיון דרגה 3 זמני, למבקש ממדינת חוץ שמתקיימים לגביו התנאים המנויים להלן (בסעיף זה – מומחה זר), לתקופה שלא תעלה על שנה (בסעיף זה – רישיון זמני):
@ref s 9(a): the Registrar may give a temporary grade 3 licence to a foreign expert who meets the conditions (src:103)
GIVEN `the day of the grant` IS A DATE
      expert IS A `Foreign expert's application under section 9`
      `in the Registrar's opinion the expert is of repute and a renowned expert in the field` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the fee was paid in full` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `An act under section 9`
`s 9(a) — the Registrar may grant a temporary licence` `the day of the grant` expert `in the Registrar's opinion the expert is of repute and a renowned expert in the field` `the fee was paid in full` MEANS
    IF       `s 9(a) — the applicant is a foreign expert meeting conditions (1) to (3)` expert `in the Registrar's opinion the expert is of repute and a renowned expert in the field`
         AND `the fee was paid in full`
    THEN PARTY `the Registrar`
         MAY `grant a temporary grade 3 licence for a term ending on` lastDay
         PROVIDED lastDay AT MOST `s 9(a) — the latest last day of a temporary licence granted on` `the day of the grant`
    ELSE FULFILLED

@ref s 9(a): whether the Registrar may give a temporary licence to the foreign expert (src:103)
@export Whether the conditions of s 9(a) for a temporary grade 3 licence are met by a foreign expert: from a foreign state; invited to work on a system above 70 kW; authorised abroad and, in the six years before the application, did installation or maintenance of similar systems; recognised by the Registrar as of repute and renowned in the field; and the fee was paid in full
GIVEN expert IS A `Foreign expert's application under section 9` @desc The expert's application and the facts s 9(a) asks of the applicant
      `in the Registrar's opinion the expert is of repute and a renowned expert in the field` IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the Registrar recognised the applicant as of repute and a renowned expert in the field
      `the fee was paid in full` IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the fee for the temporary licence was paid in full (regulation 4 of the Fees Regulations)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the temporary licence may be granted` expert `in the Registrar's opinion the expert is of repute and a renowned expert in the field` `the fee was paid in full` MEANS
        `s 9(a) — the applicant is a foreign expert meeting conditions (1) to (3)` expert `in the Registrar's opinion the expert is of repute and a renowned expert in the field`
    AND `the fee was paid in full`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- s 9(b): renewal for two further periods
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

§§ `Section 9(b) — renewal of a temporary licence`

-- FT3.  The renewal's term is counted from the last day of the term it renews (P5); the alternative counts from the day of the
-- renewal.  The last day of the term being renewed is the register's last day of validity (s 8 as composed in g2-validity):
-- a temporary licence's term is the Registrar's choice, so a temporary licence with no recorded last day gives a named refusal
-- there.
-- src:107 | {{ח:תת|(ב)}} הרשם רשאי לחדש את תוקפו של רישיון זמני לשתי תקופות נוספות שלא יעלו על שנה כל אחת.
@ref s 9(b): each further period not more than one year, from the end of the previous (src:107)
GIVEN `the last day of the term being renewed` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 9(b) — the latest last day of a term renewing one that ended on` `the last day of the term being renewed` MEANS
    `s 10(b) — the last day of a period of` 1 `years after an event on` `the last day of the term being renewed`

@ref s 9(b): each further period not more than one year, from the day of the renewal (src:107)
GIVEN `the day of the renewal` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 9(b) (counted from the day of the renewal) — the latest last day of a term renewed on` `the day of the renewal` MEANS
    `s 10(b) — the last day of a period of` 1 `years after an event on` `the day of the renewal`

-- src:107 | {{ח:תת|(ב)}} הרשם רשאי לחדש את תוקפו של רישיון זמני לשתי תקופות נוספות שלא יעלו על שנה כל אחת.
@ref s 9(b): the Registrar may renew a temporary licence for two further periods (src:107)
GIVEN licence IS A Licence
      `the fee was paid in full` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `An act under section 9`
`s 9(b) — the Registrar may renew the temporary licence` licence `the fee was paid in full` MEANS
    IF       licence's `a temporary licence under section 9`
         AND count (licence's `renewed on`) LESS THAN 2
         AND `the fee was paid in full`
    THEN PARTY `the Registrar`
         MAY `renew a temporary licence for a term ending on` lastDay
         PROVIDED lastDay AT MOST `s 9(b) — the latest last day of a term renewing one that ended on` (`s 8 — the last day of validity of the licence` licence)
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- The number of renewals still open ("two further periods").
@ref s 9(b): two further periods
GIVEN licence IS A Licence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 9(b) — the number of renewals still open to the temporary licence` licence MEANS
    IF   licence's `a temporary licence under section 9`
    THEN 2 MINUS count (licence's `renewed on`)
    ELSE 0
